# =============================================================================
# ZSMS — local development environment
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local     then fill in the values below
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored (.gitignore lines 3-8) and must never be committed
# — CONVENTIONS.md prohibition 2. This template is committed; the file you
# create from it is not.
#
# Every variable here is one the code actually reads. It was derived by grepping
# `process.env` across apps/ and packages/, not from ENV.md, because ENV.md
# lists several that nothing consumes yet (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# FIELD_ENCRYPTION_KEY, META_APP_SECRET, OPENAI_API_KEY) — those are Phase 5+.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW FAR EACH SECTION GETS YOU
#
#   Section 1 alone     → nothing. Every API route 401s: no session, no token.
#   Sections 1 + 2      → the admin dashboard runs against the real seed data.
#                         THIS IS ALL YOU NEED RIGHT NOW.
#   Section 3 onwards   → workers, uploads, real message delivery. Phase 6.
#
# Turborepo reads `.env` / `.env.local` from the REPO ROOT for the vars listed
# in turbo.json's globalEnv. Put this file at the root, not in apps/web.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# 1. SUPABASE  —  required
#
# Dashboard → project `zsms-dev` (ref tevblmcebsqqjgzjptgw) → Settings → API
# https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/tevblmcebsqqjgzjptgw/settings/api
# =============================================================================

# "Project URL". Should be exactly this for zsms-dev — spelled out so a typo in
# the ref shows up here rather than as a confusing DNS failure.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://tevblmcebsqqjgzjptgw.supabase.co

# "Project API keys" → `anon` / `public` (newer dashboards: "publishable").
# NOT a secret: it ships to every browser by design and grants nothing on its
# own — RLS decides everything, and `anon` has been REVOKEd from every tenant
# table in this schema. Safe in a client bundle; still not committed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...replace-me

# "Project API keys" → `service_role`. **This one IS a secret.** It bypasses RLS
# entirely.
#
# NOT NEEDED for the admin dashboard, deliberately: apps/web has no code path
# that reads it. lib/supabase.ts has no createServiceClient and its header
# explains why. Only the Railway workers use it, under ADR-042. Leave commented
# out unless you are running `npm run dev:workers`.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...replace-me


# =============================================================================
# 2. CLERK  —  required for anything past a 401
#
# Dashboard → your DEVELOPMENT instance → API Keys
# https://dashboard.clerk.com   (pick the dev instance, not production)
#
# Development keys are prefixed pk_test_ / sk_test_. A pk_live_ here means you
# are pointed at production users.
# =============================================================================

CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...replace-me

# Nothing in the repo reads this yet — there is no sign-in UI, so the Clerk
# Next.js middleware has not been wired up. Set it now anyway: it is the name
# the provider will look for, and it costs nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...replace-me

# Which provider packages/auth-provider instantiates. `clerk` is the only
# implementation that exists; `keycloak` is the self-hosted path (ADR-007) and
# is not built.
AUTH_PROVIDER=clerk

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLERK SETUP THAT IS NOT A VARIABLE — this is the part that bites
#
# Supabase has to accept Clerk's JWT, and Clerk has to put the claims the RLS
# helpers read into it. Neither happens by default.
#
#  a) Clerk → Configure → Sessions → Customise session token.
#     Migration 0001's helpers read `o.id`, `o.slg`, `o.rol`, and `sub`.
#     CLERK.md carries the exact template.
#
#  b) Supabase → Authentication → Sign In / Providers → add Clerk as a
#     third-party auth provider, using your Clerk Frontend API domain.
#
#  c) To see the ADMIN dashboard you must belong to a Clerk organisation whose
#     slug is exactly:
#
#         afritech-systems-admin
#
#     That string is the entire definition of "platform admin" —
#     is_afritech_admin() in the database and resolveAdminContext() in the API
#     both test it and nothing else. Create the org, add yourself, done. Any
#     other slug gives a 403, which is correct behaviour rather than a bug.
#
#  d) The seeded schools carry clerk_org_id values org_test_a … org_test_f.
#     Those are placeholders, not real Clerk org IDs. A school-portal login
#     will not resolve to a seeded school until you either create matching
#     Clerk orgs or update schools.clerk_org_id to real ones. This does NOT
#     affect the admin dashboard, which reads across schools rather than
#     through a membership.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# =============================================================================
# 3. COUNTRY AND URLS  —  optional, defaults exist
# =============================================================================

NEXT_PUBLIC_COUNTRY_CODE=ZM

# Absolute base for logo URLs in transactional email. A mail client cannot
# resolve a relative path, and localhost renders as a broken image in every
# inbox that receives it — so this defaults to https://zsms.co.zm rather than
# to your dev host. Override only when testing email through a public tunnel.
# ZSMS_PUBLIC_URL=https://zsms.co.zm
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ZSMS_URL=http://localhost:3000


# =============================================================================
# 4. WORKERS AND QUEUE  —  only for `npm run dev:workers`
#
# There is no Redis on this machine, so a worker starts and idles. Nothing has
# round-tripped through BullMQ yet — Phase 6, see CLAUDE.md's Phase 3 caveat.
# The web app needs none of this.
# =============================================================================

# JOB_QUEUE_PROVIDER=bullmq
# BULLMQ_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# QSTASH_TOKEN=


# =============================================================================
# 5. NOTIFICATIONS  —  Phase 6, with credentials
#
# Unset, every channel resolves to the mock provider and nothing leaves this
# machine. That is the current state and it is deliberate.
# =============================================================================

# `mock` | `live`. Leave unset for mock.
# NOTIFICATION_PROVIDER=mock
# Name a channel to force it to fail — exercises the fallback chain without
# needing a real provider to break.
# NOTIFICATION_MOCK_FAIL=

# META_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# META_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@zsms.co.zm
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=


# =============================================================================
# 6. CLOUDFLARE R2  —  file storage, Phase 6
#
# Two buckets. PUBLIC holds school logos; PRIVATE holds receipts and report
# cards, which name a child and an amount. The admin dashboard needs neither —
# the school-portal logo upload will be the first consumer.
# =============================================================================

# R2_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT=
# R2_PUBLIC_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_PUBLIC_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_PUBLIC_BUCKET_NAME=

# R2_PRIVATE_ENDPOINT=
# R2_PRIVATE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_PRIVATE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_PRIVATE_BUCKET_NAME=
